    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0318" n="904" xml:id="pg904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 PW (Peace)/11–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Korea
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-23T19:00:00-05:00">November 23,
                            1949—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>984. For Ambassador.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d166-f1"/> For ur conf info, current
                    thinking in Dept is that all nations which
                    declared war or state of belligerency against Jap shld be party to Jap peace
                    treaty. It is envisaged 13 FEC countries wld be
                    actual negotiating powers, with remaining 38 nations to participate in
                    consultative capacity.</p>
                <p>Present draft makes no provision for inclusion ROK in either category.</p>
                <p>
                    Dept wld appreciate ur views urgently as to
                    whether and to what extent provision shld be made for Korean participation in
                    Jap treaty, in terms both of domestic political considerations and of probable
                    substantive effect on negotiation of peace settlement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
